 Located in Đakovo, Croatia\n\nThe most famous basilica named after Saint Peter is clearly **St. Peter's Basilica** located in **Vatican City** (which is within Rome, Italy). This is the most prominent and internationally known basilica named after Saint Peter.\n\n\nI have identified five basilicas dedicated to Saint Peter across different locations, with St. Peter's Basilica in Vatican City being the most prominent.\n</think>\n\nBased on the documents, I found several basilicas/churches named after Saint Peter:\n\n1. **St. Peter's Basilica** (The Papal Basilica of St. Peter in the Vatican) - This is the most prominent basilica named after Saint Peter. It is located in **Vatican City**, the papal enclave within the city of Rome.\n\n2. **Church of San Pietro in Montorio** - Located in Rome (on Janiculum hill)\n\n3. **San Pietro, Modena** - A monastery and church complex in Modena, Italy\n\n4. **San Pietro a Ovile** - A medieval church in Siena, Italy\n\n5. **Đakovo Cathedral** (Cathedral basilica of St. Peter) - Located in Đakovo, Croatia\n\n**Answer:** The main basilica named after Saint Peter is **St. Peter's Basilica** (also called the Papal Basilica of St. Peter in the Vatican), and it is located in **Vatican City** (within Rome, Italy).\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_21bf724fcffeZtFj6dKZ5MZvfH","model":{"modelID":"qwen35-9b","providerID":"local"},"truncated":false},"title":"Find Basilica of St. Peter and its city","time":{"start":1777647278845,"end":1777647305530}}}}
